<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/" xmlns:dmndi="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/DMNDI/" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DC/" xmlns:modeler="http://camunda.org/schema/modeler/1.0" id="Definitions_0092biv" name="DRD" namespace="http://camunda.org/schema/1.0/dmn" exporter="Camunda Modeler" exporterVersion="5.41.0" modeler:executionPlatform="Camunda Cloud" modeler:executionPlatformVersion="8.8.0">
  <description>Ocular Prophylaxis for Gonococcal Ophthalmia Neonatorum

USPSTF Grade A Recommendation:
"The USPSTF recommends prophylactic ocular topical medication for all newborns to prevent gonococcal ophthalmia neonatorum."

Medication (USPSTF):
- 0.5% erythromycin ophthalmic ointment (only FDA-approved option in US)

Timing: "Shortly after birth" — infection can cause severe damage as early as 24 hours after birth.

Trigger: Evaluate at birth and on each chart access until prophylaxis is documented (named-event: birth, encounter-start). This persistent reminder pattern ensures prophylaxis is not forgotten in complicated deliveries or unit transfers.

Glossary:
- OcularProphylaxisAdministered: True if prophylactic eye medication has been documented as given. Includes erythromycin (US), or WHO alternatives: tetracycline, povidone iodine, silver nitrate, chloramphenicol.

Context: Live newborn delivered in a hospital or other modern healthcare facility.

WHO Alternative (WHO Recommendations on Newborn Health, 2017):
"For all neonates, the WHO STI guideline recommends topical ocular prophylaxis for the prevention of gonococcal and chlamydial ophthalmia neonatorum." (Strong recommendation)
WHO-approved agents: tetracycline 1%, erythromycin 0.5%, povidone iodine 2.5% (water-based), silver nitrate 1%, chloramphenicol 1%.

Note: No correlate found in MADiE eCQMs or WHO SMART guidelines.

Sources:
- https://www.uspreventiveservicestaskforce.org/uspstf/recommendation/ocular-prophylaxis-for-gonococcal-ophthalmia-neonatorum-preventive-medication
- WHO Recommendations on Newborn Health (2017)</description>
  <decision id="Decision_1ry6f6f" name="Ocular Prophylaxis for Gonococcal Ophthalmia Neonatorum">
    <decisionTable id="DecisionTable_0rpbv0a">
      <input id="Input_1" label="Ocular Prophylaxis Administered">
        <inputExpression id="InputExpression_1" typeRef="boolean">
          <text>OcularProphylaxisAdministered</text>
        </inputExpression>
      </input>
      <output id="Output_1" label="Administer Ocular Prophylaxis" name="AdministerOcularProphylaxis" typeRef="boolean" />
      <rule id="DecisionRule_0dkmck5">
        <description>Prophylaxis not yet documented: Recommend administration. USPSTF: "prophylactic ocular topical medication for all newborns." Alert persists until action is documented — ensures prophylaxis is not forgotten in complicated deliveries or unit transfers.</description>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1j4tita">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_0onrdp7">
          <text>true</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="DecisionRule_1aqyevv">
        <description>Prophylaxis already documented: No further action needed. Task complete — alert clears.</description>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_05umtj6">
          <text>true</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_1m29h8x">
          <text>false</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
    </decisionTable>
  </decision>
  <dmndi:DMNDI>
    <dmndi:DMNDiagram>
      <dmndi:DMNShape dmnElementRef="Decision_1ry6f6f">
        <dc:Bounds height="80" width="180" x="160" y="100" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
    </dmndi:DMNDiagram>
  </dmndi:DMNDI>
</definitions>
